{%- comment -%}
  Results fragment for the cart's "להשלים את הערכה" (snippets/cart-upsell).

  Fetched as /search?q=<query>&type=product&options[prefix]=last&section_id=cart-upsell and printed
  as bare tiles; assets/cart-upsell.js moves them into the list in the drawer and on the cart page.
  The shell is a snippet, so this file is only ever the fragment.

  Why search and not a collection: the case that fits "iPhone 17 Pro Max" sits inside a
  3,390-product accessories collection, and Liquid cannot filter a collection by title. The store's
  titles put the model after "ל-", which the search engine indexes. /search/suggest answers 417 to
  Hebrew on this store, so the Section Rendering API is the route.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if search.performed and search.terms != blank -%}
  {%- paginate search.results by 24 -%}
    {%- assign cu_shown = 0 -%}
    {%- for cu_item in search.results -%}
      {%- liquid
        # Eight, not four: the script drops what is already in the cart and merges two queries, so it
        # needs more candidates than it will show.
        if cu_shown >= 8
          break
        endif
        assign cu_ok = false
        if cu_item.object_type == 'product'
          if cu_item.available
            assign cu_type = cu_item.type | strip
            assign cu_head = cu_type | slice: 0, 2
            if cu_head == 'א.'
              assign cu_ok = true
            endif
          endif
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if cu_ok -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign cu_variant = cu_item.selected_or_first_available_variant
          assign cu_compare = 0
          if cu_variant.compare_at_price > cu_variant.price
            assign cu_compare = cu_variant.compare_at_price
          endif
          assign cu_shown = cu_shown | plus: 1
        -%}
        <li
          class="cu-card"
          data-cu-item
          data-cu-handle="{{ cu_item.handle }}"
          data-cu-variant="{{ cu_variant.id }}"
        >
          <a class="cu-card__link" href="{{ cu_item.url }}">
            {%- comment -%}
              Most of these accessories have no photo in Shopify — measured on the live catalogue:
              86% of the cases, 94% of the screen protectors and 76% of the chargers — so the well
              falls back to the JOY symbol rather than printing nothing.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="cu-card__media">
              {%- if cu_item.featured_media != blank -%}
                {%- render 'image',
                  image: cu_item.featured_media.preview_image,
                  widths: '120,240',
                  sizes: '60px',
                  decorative: true,
                  class: 'cu-card__img'
                -%}
              {%- else -%}
                <img
                  class="cu-card__img cu-card__img--fallback"
                  src="{{ 'logo-joy-symbol.png' | asset_url }}"
                  alt=""
                  width="361"
                  height="472"
                  loading="lazy"
                >
              {%- endif -%}
            </span>
            <span class="cu-card__title">{{ cu_item.title | escape }}</span>
          </a>

          {%- comment -%}
            Price and button sit at the foot in normal flow. The button was a circle positioned over
            the price row, and at tile width that put it through the price and over the card's own
            border -- and a bare "+" never said it was a button at all.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="cu-card__foot">
            <p class="cu-card__prices">
              <span class="cu-card__price">{{ cu_variant.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
              {%- if cu_compare > 0 -%}
                <s class="cu-card__was">{{ cu_compare | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</s>
              {%- endif -%}
            </p>

            {%- comment -%}
              One press adds it. In a cart there is nothing left to decide, so a tick box and a
              second "add" press would only put a step between the shopper and what they want.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <button
              class="cu-card__add"
              type="button"
              data-cu-add
              aria-label="{{ 'cart.upsell.add_label' | t: title: cu_item.title }}"
            >
              <span class="cu-card__state cu-card__state--idle">
                {%- render 'icon', name: 'plus', size: 14 -%}
                {{- 'cart.upsell.add' | t -}}
              </span>
              <span class="cu-card__state cu-card__state--done">
                {%- render 'icon', name: 'check', size: 14 -%}
                {{- 'cart.upsell.in_cart' | t -}}
              </span>
            </button>
          </div>
        </li>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endpaginate -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "תוספות בעגלה (תוצאות)",
  "tag": "div",
  "class": "section-cart-upsell-results",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
